COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the scene fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge as a single full-bleed image — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block. The lower two-fifths is the same continuous scene rendered dark, smoky and low in detail so overlay text stays readable, while all faces, flags and key objects sit entirely within the upper three-fifths. photorealistic news-crisis composite, dramatic hard lighting, heavy atmospheric haze, one dominant colour drowning the frame, the upper three-fifths densely packed with elements, cinematic wide-angle, high contrast and eye-catching. An enormous Chinese flag — red field with one large yellow star and four smaller stars — hangs across the whole background in deep heavy folds rather than flying taut, pronounced creases catching the light, its red saturated and crisply lit from a hard side light, the star pattern fully intact and readable. In front of it, occupying the right third at chest-up scale, stands Xi Jinping (President of China), no hands in frame, chin slightly lifted, eyes narrowed and level, lips closed in a flat controlled line, a hard orange key light raking across one side of his face. Filling the centre-left, a single colossal semiconductor wafer-handling line runs into the distance, its robotic arms and stacked wafer carriers glowing hot crimson through the haze, thin smoke drifting low along the floor. Deep red and ember orange drown the frame; the sky above is dark and smoke-choked. no text, no letters, no words, no numbers, no captions, no watermark.

